98	  /// The basename of `argv[0]` as the process was originally exec'd (e.g. `claude`, `vim`), or nil
99	  /// if it can't be resolved. Deliberately NOT `proc_name`/`p_comm`: some CLIs (Claude Code among
100	  /// them, observed in the wild) rename their own process title after launch — `p_comm` then reads
101	  /// as their version string ("2.1.232"), not the command a user typed. `KERN_PROCARGS2` returns
102	  /// the ORIGINAL exec-time argv snapshot, unaffected by any later self-renaming, and matches what
103	  /// the shell's own preexec title-report already uses for a live (non-reattached) pane.
104	  static func executableName(processID: pid_t) -> String? {
